{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and G2 models its motion capabilities. The specifications E1-E4 enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: E1 binds clear perception to forward/random_walk actions, E2 and E3 enforce directed recovery turns for left/right obstacles, and E4 enforces conservative backward recovery only for front obstacles. All obstacle events force a recovery state before resuming exploration. The design ensures the robot spends most time exploring, recovers quickly, and avoids unsafe oscillations or repeated backward motions.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for modularity.",
    "Use specification automata to bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and quick return to exploration."
  ],
